<!-- FAQ -->
<div style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;padding:100px 40px">
  <div class="reveal">
    <div class="section-label">Questions</div>
    <div class="section-title">FAQ</div>
  </div>
  <div id="faq" class="reveal">
    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Do I need videos to learn? <span class="faq-chevron">▼</span></div>
      <div class="faq-a">Every lesson is delivered as a dynamically generated 1,500+ word deep-dive, built fresh for each student. Video slots are built into the platform - as video content is recorded and published, it will automatically appear alongside the text lesson. You can learn fully without video. Video is an enhancement, not a requirement.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Why is every lesson different? <span class="faq-chevron">▼</span></div>
      <div class="faq-a">The platform generates fresh lesson content every time based on the topic, your student ID, and a unique session seed. This means no two students get the same content, retakes get entirely new material, and the platform never gets "gamed" by sharing answers. This is how education at scale should work.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">What if I fail the final exam? <span class="faq-chevron">▼</span></div>
      <div class="faq-a">You can retake the final exam. Your retake gets a completely new set of 50 final exam questions. Your progress (completed lessons and module scores) is preserved, so you only need to retake the final - not the entire course.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Is this accredited? <span class="faq-chevron">▼</span></div>
      <div class="faq-a">MarkCMO Academy is a professional development platform, not an accredited academic institution. The diploma is a credential of professional excellence from Mark Donnigan, a recognized Fractional CMO and business growth expert. The rigor is by design - you cannot fake your way through a 50-question final exam with new questions every retake. The value comes from what you actually learn and can prove you know.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">How long do courses take? <span class="faq-chevron">▼</span></div>
      <div class="faq-a">Most courses are 35-80 hours of study time. You go at your own pace - there are no deadlines or time limits. The average student completes a course in 4-12 weeks. Access is lifetime, so you can return and review any lesson whenever you need a refresher.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Can I take multiple courses? <span class="faq-chevron">▼</span></div>
      <div class="faq-a">Absolutely. Each course is independent - you can start any course at any time. Many students start with the CMO or COO course and add LinkedIn, Digital Marketing, and Revenue Architecture as they scale their practice.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

